From: sofent <hengzhen@echooo.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: skip empty trailing fragments on TX

On NanoPi R2S, the DWMAC1000 TX DMA can stall on a zero-length
last descriptor. The TX FIFO still contains data, but the frame
does not complete and the watchdog resets the adapter.

Trim empty trailing fragments from the local descriptor count before
allocating ring entries. The existing TX path then marks the last
data descriptor as the frame end, including the linear-only case.
Leave the skb fragment list intact for normal release.

Signed-off-by: sofent <hengzhen@echooo.xyz>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -4537,6 +4537,12 @@
 		priv->xstats.max_sdu_txq_drop[queue]++;
 		goto max_sdu_err;
 	}
+
+	/* A zero-length final segment cannot complete on DWMAC1000.
+	 * Keep the skb's fragment references intact for normal skb release.
+	 */
+	while (nfrags && !skb_frag_size(&skb_shinfo(skb)->frags[nfrags - 1]))
+		nfrags--;
 
 	if (unlikely(stmmac_tx_avail(priv, queue) < nfrags + 1)) {
 		if (!netif_tx_queue_stopped(netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, queue))) {
